# Netlify Redirects
# Astro is configured with `trailingSlash: 'never'` (see astro.config.mjs),
# so URLs are canonicalized at build time. Do NOT add a generic
# trailing-slash normalization rule like `/*/ /:splat 301!` here — in
# Netlify's _redirects syntax the splat `*` is intended for use at the end
# of the source path, and using it mid-path also matches paths WITHOUT a
# trailing slash, producing an infinite redirect loop (ERR_TOO_MANY_REDIRECTS).

